tually made  from fruits we think that it's a healthy  choice okay all the Edit sugar ruins  everything but we can easily forget  about that quinoa it is now one of the  most popular choices when someone wants  to  eat something healthy but how can you  say that you pay attention to everything  that you eat when you don't even know  how it grows the protein-packed seed is  actually harvested from tall green  plants the plant sprouts are slowly  growing at first but they eventually  shoot to 3 feet the part of the quinoa  plant that we usually eat is the seed  the leaves of the plants are also edible  so it would be a good idea to try them  in a salad what is impressive about this  plant is that it can be cultivated in  high-risk areas as it is tolerant to  cold salt wind and frost now we  understand why it's so popular dates if  you think that dates grow on a calendar  you probably didn't understand that  right anyway you probably didn't care  about edible dates because they are the  least popular dry fruits at the grocery  store we want to give them some love and  this is why I will tell you some fun  facts about them people are really  motivated when it comes to harvesting  this unwelcome fruit because it actually  grows at the top of very high palm trees  up to 75 feet high dates are found in  big clusters just underneath the palms  fronds and it just looks weird we hope  that you are not afraid of heights  because it will take a lot of courage to  climb there sesame seeds we always see  sesame seeds on bagels and hamburger  buns so we have to admit that we once  thought it was just part of the bread  when we were kids but now we obviously  all know that it grows in nature  actually it shouldn't be so surprising  because there is the word seed in the  name the sesame plant native to Asia and  East Africa grows fruits the long pod is  then dried and this is when it starts to  open revealing the seeds inside the  plant is then shaken to release the  seeds however we are still wondering  about one thing how these sesame seeds  even stay in place on hamburger buns  there must be a sesame glue or something  cranberries you probably think that you  already know how this fruit grows after  all you've always seen it growing in  water right actually it's only one part  of the process  technically cranberries just grow on  vines like strawberries all they need is  a special combination of soil and water  properties the reason why they grow  underwater is to protect them from cold  temperature during winter in the spring  the field is strained and the  cranberries will be back underwater  again when the time comes to harvest  them they just have to knock the berries  off the vines and they will start  floating this is just the proof that you  shouldn't only look at one picture to  know the full story vanilla most of us  didn't even think that vanilla could  grow we first thought it was just a  little taste of heaven added in our  favorite ice cream or our birthday cake  but did you know that vanilla actually  comes from an orchid so in nature it  looks like a really pretty flower the  vine can grow up to 30 feet long and the  vanilla plant folia is the only plant  used for industrial food production but  the part that we usually eat the pod  looks more like a green bean they are  picked before they are ripe and plunged  in hot water and then dried for up to  six months this is how we end up with  this black thing we didn't expect  vanilla to be a pod that is so old  pineapples contrary to popular beliefs  pineapples don't grow into the sea and  no sponge lives in them and they don't  grow on trees either  they are right in the middle as they  grow out of the ground from a leaky  plant we think that it just looks like  someone dropped a fruit on a poor little  plant but a healthy pineapple plant can  have leaves up to five feet long the  fruit grows out the top of the central  stem and is actually the result of  dozens of individual fruit producing  flowers that are fused into a single  fruit we just have a weird feeling every  time we look at a field full of  pineapple plants cinnamon if we asked  you to guess what cinnamon looks like we  think that it would take you a lot of  time to get the right answer that's  because it doesn't look like any other  plant on this list but more like a  simple tree actually it comes from the  inner layer of bark derived from  evergreen trees the farmers shaved the  outer bark of the trees and then the  inner bark which is the cinnamon layer  they then dry it out for use this is  when it curls up in quills which are  then crushed into a spice powder cut  into sticks now we think that you can  recognize it cashews when we first took  a look at cashews we were  wondering how they actually grow if they  ever grow at all it turns out that this  nut grows from a faucet that looks like  a red apple the cashew itself is  actually the real fruit the fake fruit  is also edible and is often made into  beverages or Jam but we all know that  nothing is more popular than the cashew  itself but you shouldn't eat them in  nature because their shells contain an  acid that causes allergies and reactions  similar to poison ivy have you ever  wondered how any other popular fruit  grows don't be shy to share your  thoughts in the comment section down  below we love to hear what you think and  that's it for what popular foods look  like before they're harvested for more  stories like this make sure you watch 10  foods you'll never buy again knowing how  they are made thanks for watching  [Music]
 

